 "wiki": {
  "title": "Kinyongia uthmoelleri",
  "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kinyongia_uthmoelleri",
  "revision": 1355109097,
  "sections": [
   {
    "h": null,
    "level": 1,
    "paras": [
     "Kinyongia uthmoelleri, known commonly as the Hanang hornless chameleon, Müller's leaf chameleon, and Uthmöller's chameleon, is species of lizard in the family Chamaeleonidae. The species is endemic to Tanzania."
    ]
   },
   {
    "h": "Etymology",
    "level": 2,
    "paras": [
     "The specific name, uthmoelleri, is in honor of German herpetologist Wolfgang Uthmöller."
    ]
   },
   {
    "h": "Habitat",
    "level": 2,
    "paras": [
     "The preferred natural habitat of Kinyongia uthmoelleri is forest, at altitudes of 1,700–2,500 m (5,600–8,200 ft)."
    ]
   },
   {
    "h": "Description",
    "level": 2,
    "paras": [
     "The maximum recorded size for Kinyongia uthmoelleri is a male with a total length (tail included) of 22.7 cm (8.9 in)."
    ]
   },
   {
    "h": "Reproduction",
    "level": 2,
    "paras": [
     "Kinyongia uthmoelleri is oviparous."
    ]
   },
   {
    "h": "Subspecies",
    "level": 2,
    "paras": [
     "Two subspecies are recognized as being valid, including the nominotypical subspecies.",
     "Kinyongia uthmoelleri artytor Lutzmann, Stipala, Lademann, Krause, Wilms & Schmitz, 2010",
     "Kinyongia uthmoelleri uthmoelleri L. Müller, 1938"
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
